<title>POLAND: Polish T-bill minimum prices rise on large demand.</title>
<headline>Polish T-bill minimum prices rise on large demand.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>All minimum prices of Polish T-bills rose at today's primary auction on total demand of 2.3 billion zlotys against a 1.3 billion zloty offer, the finance ministry said.  </p>
<p>   T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week 52-week</p>
<p>   new min price     --     94.98    90.24	--     82.21</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)     --    (94.97)  (90.22)     --    (82.18)</p>
<p>   new max price     --     95.29    90.45	--     82.45</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)     --    (95.05)  (90.43)     --    (82.34)</p>
<p>   offer		 --     400.0    300.0	--     600.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded     --     513.8    562.6	--   1,197.5</p>
<p>   bids accepted     --     400.0    300.0	--     600.0</p>
<p>   next auction    200.0    300.0    100.0	--     600.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
